# SECTION 3 — THE STORM   b53-92   (1:40 - 2:50)
# Phrase (8 bars) i | i6 | bVI(maj7) | bVII | i | iv | bVIsus4 | bVI7 ;
# bVI7 is V7 of the key a semitone up:  Dm -> Ebm -> Em -> Fm -> F#m.
# Full kumi-daiko: shime ji-uchi, chu-daiko I 3+3+2, chu-daiko II
# interlocking ka/don, O-daiko punctuation, atarigane from Ebm.  Brass
# stabs only off the beat.  THEME (horns from Em): the ARP motif turned
# into a melody (d-a | g-f | f-d | e ...).  F#m ends on its bVI = D major:
# one blow and the drums vanish.

# -- full kumi-daiko: shime ji-uchi, chu-daiko 3+3+2 + interlocking ka, O-daiko
# -- punctuation; brass stabs off the beat; every 8 bars up a semitone
# -- (bar 8 = bVI7 of the old key = V7 of the new one).
== b53-60 [Storm] ==
